.TH FAST2BAN-SERVER "1" "October 2026" "Fast2Ban v0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fast2ban-server \- Fast2Ban daemon server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fast2ban-server
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBFast2Ban\fR is a high-performance Rust rewrite of Fail2Ban. It monitors system
logs and systemd journals for security authentication failures and bans offending IP
addresses by orchestrating packet filter firewall rules.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR <DIR>
Configuration directory (default: \fI/etc/fail2ban\fR).
.TP
\fB\-s\fR <FILE>
Unix domain socket path (default: \fI/var/run/fail2ban/fail2ban.sock\fR).
.TP
\fB\-p\fR <FILE>
PID file path (default: \fI/var/run/fail2ban/fail2ban.pid\fR).
.TP
\fB\-f\fR
Start server in foreground (default runs in background).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Display help message.
.SH "SECURITY & PRIVILEGE MODEL"
\fBfast2ban-server\fR runs with strict umask (0077) ensuring all socket and PID files
are accessible only by the owning root user. Untrusted log data interpolated into action
templates is automatically escaped via shell parameters, preventing command injection.
Pickle protocol decoding is strictly sandboxed to primitive data types only.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
fast2ban-client(1), fast2ban-regex(1), jail.conf(5)
